=== dream.arrival
@title Behind the Closed Eye

{image("dream-hall.jpeg", "An expedition table and a solitary explorer stand on still dark water in a hall of mist.")}

The stone vanishes beneath your hand. You stand in a hall without walls.
{player:pronoun#capitalize} {player:pronoun#one-many("has", "have")} crossed without moving a foot.

A woman sits at a table laid for eight, counting cups.

-> dream.hub

=== dream.hub
@title The Hall Without Walls
@hub all(dream,keeper)
@hub-limit 2

The keepers wait around the table. Glyph marks held: **{var:marks}**.
Three will let you approach the shape sleeping beneath it.

* [Wake before going further] -> dream.wake

=== dream.ines
@title Speak to the lost explorer
@tags dream,keeper
@priority 30
@once

~ var:sum = (6 + 2) * 3 / 2 - 1
~ var:sum -= 1

> ines: Six plus two. Three times. Half. Less one, less one. {var:sum}.

Her collar still bears the name **{ines:name}**.
{if visited(camp.guide)}
You recognize the explorer from {guide:first-name#possessive} story.
{/if}

{if var:sum == 10 and var:sum != 0}
> ines: Ten steps in. Nine steps out. One stays. Tell {guide:first-name} I remember the river.
{/if}

* [Promise to carry her message] -> dream.hub

=== dream.spiral
@title Answer the Spiral
@tags dream,keeper
@priority 20
@once

{spiral:first-name#capitalize} turns without moving. {spiral:pronoun#capitalize}
{spiral:pronoun#one-many("has", "have")} a question; the answer should be yours.

> spiral: What is the watchword?

{if var:watchword == ""}
> spiral: A retired word leaves no echo. Silence is an honest answer.
{else}
{if var:watch-note == ""}
> spiral: "{var:watchword}"? A suggestion, never recorded. You have not yet agreed on who should answer.
{else}
{if var:watchword == var:watch-note}
> spiral: "{var:watchword}". The living voice and the written word agree. I know you.
{else}
> spiral: The page says "{var:watch-note}"; you say "{var:watchword}". You changed the word, not the ink.
{/if}
{/if}
{/if}

{spiral:pronoun#capitalize} opens {spiral:pronoun:possessive-pronoun:determiner} palm.

* [Accept the spiral mark] { take spiral glyph-mark; give player glyph-mark; var:marks += 1 } -> dream.hub

=== dream.watcher
@title Face the Watcher
@tags dream,keeper
@requires player has glyph-mark
@priority 10
@once

{watcher:first-name#capitalize} unfolds above the table.
{watcher:pronoun#capitalize} {watcher:pronoun#one-many("has", "have")} no eyelid.

::: skill-check watcher perception dc 15
success: { set flag:watcher-saw } -> dream.watcher-sees
failure: -> dream.watcher-missed
:::

=== dream.watcher-sees
@title Under the Eye

> watcher: I see the waking world caught in your hair.

-> dream.watcher-choice

=== dream.watcher-missed
@title Between Glances

> watcher: Something crossed the threshold. Was it you?

-> dream.watcher-choice

=== dream.watcher-choice
@title A Way Past the Eye

{if flag:watcher-saw}
The eye follows every movement.
{else}
You have a moment before its gaze returns.
{/if}

* [Remember that you are dreaming] skill-check lucidity dc 14
  success: -> dream.eye-mark
  failure: -> dream.watcher-failed
* [Slip beneath its gaze] skill-check stealth dc 13
  success: -> dream.eye-mark
  failure: -> dream.watcher-failed
* [Meet its gaze without flinching] (requires: player:courage >= 6) -> dream.eye-mark
* [Wake rather than face it] -> dream.wake

=== dream.watcher-failed
@title A Fraying Thought

The hall stretches away. You gather yourself before trying another way.

-> dream.watcher-choice

=== dream.eye-mark
@title The Open Eye

~ take watcher glyph-mark
~ give player glyph-mark
~ var:marks += 1

{watcher:first-name#capitalize} lowers its gaze. A second glyph mark rests in your palm.

-> dream.hub

=== dream.archivist
@title Hear the guild ghost
@tags dream,keeper
@priority 5
@once

{archivist:first-name#capitalize} wears a guild coat with no body inside it.

{if faction:explorers-guild >= friendly}
> archivist: They still put your name in the ledger. Make them write ours there too.
{else}
{if faction:explorers-guild >= neutral}
> archivist: The guild sent us here, then forgot the cost.
{else}
> archivist: You know what it is to fall out of their favour. Do not let them erase us.
{/if}
{/if}

* [Promise the guild an honest account] (requires: faction:explorers-guild >= neutral) { set flag:dream-promise; faction:explorers-guild += 5 } -> dream.hub
* [Refuse to speak for the guild] { faction:explorers-guild -= 10 } -> dream.hub

=== dream.hands
@title Ask the Hands for passage
@tags dream,keeper
@requires visited(dream.eye-mark) and var:marks == 2
@priority 0
@once

{hands:first-name#capitalize} {hands:pronoun#one-many("has", "have")} no owner.
{hands:pronoun#capitalize} {hands:pronoun#one-many("offers", "offer")} the final mark.

> hands: Three to reach the Sleeper. One to us when you leave. That is our price.

* [Accept the hand mark and the price] { take hands glyph-mark; give player glyph-mark; var:marks += 1 } -> dream.hub
* [Refuse and wake] -> dream.wake

=== dream.sleeper
@title Approach the Sleeper
@tags dream,keeper
@requires var:marks == 3 and flag:all-marks and player has glyph-mark
@priority -10
@once

{if player:lucidity >= 5}
{image("sleeper-high.jpeg", "Beneath an expedition table, a stone doorway is clearly visible beyond a pale-gold disc on its threshold.")}

You see {sleeper:first-name} clearly: not a monster, but an opening waiting for someone to mistake it for a door.
> sleeper: The relic is the latch. Carry it if you must. Never turn it.
{else}
{if player:lucidity >= 2}
{image("sleeper-middle.jpeg", "A stone doorway, a pale disc and an indistinct dark shape emerge through mist beneath an expedition table.")}

A shape stirs beneath the table. You catch a warning about the relic, a latch, and a door that must stay shut.
{else}
{image("sleeper-low.jpeg", "Impenetrable shadow fills the space beneath an expedition table, obscuring whatever lies beyond.")}

You cannot hold the shape in mind. Only its hunger remains when you look away.
{/if}
{/if}

* [Pay the Hands and return to the temple] (requires: var:marks == 3) { take player glyph-mark; give hands glyph-mark; var:marks -= 1; set flag:dream-opened; player:xp += 50 } -> dream.passage

=== dream.passage
@title The Price of Waking

{hands:first-name#capitalize} close around the mark. Their price is paid.
You keep **{var:marks}** marks and the memory of what sleeps inside.
The stone door opens beneath your hand.

-> temple.hall

=== dream.wake
@title The Unopened Door

The cold stone is solid again. {guide:first-name} catches your arm.
The dream has not opened the door; the other ways in remain.

-> temple.door
